    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0522" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg416"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July 8,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 637.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has to commend your efforts
                    toward securing due protection for our citizens in China, whose lives were
                    endangered by the late riots, as reported in your No. 1314, of the 28th of May
                    last, acknowledging at the same time your No. 1311 of 25th, and your No. 1312 of
                    27th of May, relating particulars of the riots.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
